    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "you say that, but it feels like a polite consolation. it's not about the foundation, it's about the fact that the intellectual pursuit itself has changed. there's no more discovery, just calculation. i look at my hands and i don't see a scholar anymore, i just see an old man taking up space in a world that doesn't have a use for his specific kind of thinking. it feels very... heavy. like i'm holding onto a rope that's already been cut.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
